## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical sliding-window counting and maintaining top-k with bounded memory.

## Key Concepts
- Sliding window data structure
- Hashmap for counts
- Top-k extraction in bounded time
- Deterministic tie-breaking

## Code Example
````javascript
// Sketch
const W = 10000;
const windowQ = [];
const counts = new Map();
function applyBatch(batch){
  for (const x of batch){
    windowQ.push(x);
    counts.set(x, (counts.get(x) || 0) + 1);
    if (windowQ.length > W){
      const y = windowQ.shift();
      const ny = (counts.get(y) - 1);
      if (ny) counts.set(y, ny);
      else counts.delete(y);
    }
  }
  const top3 = [...counts.entries()].sort((a,b)=>b[1]-a[1]).slice(0,3).map(e=>e[0]);
  return top3;
}
````

